所以，我想这就是他实现这一愿望的方式。

487
00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:27.340
But Marv was not interested in reading his premature obituary.
但马夫对阅读自己提前发布的讣告并不感兴趣。

488
00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:28.080
It bummed him out.
这让他很沮丧。

489
00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:28.940
It really did.
确实如此。

490
00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:33.560
Now we have a little sort of runner of people reacting to Marv being in the bullpen.
现在我们有一个小插曲，讲的是大家对马夫出现在新闻编辑室里的反应。

491
00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:35.340
Like, Detrick freezes around him.
比如，德特里克在他身边时会僵住。

492
00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:39.040
Atalola says, oh, I don't, like, suck up to people.
阿塔洛拉说，哦，我不喜欢拍马屁。

493
00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:42.280
But then she's, like, super overly chipper and smiley.
但随后她表现得超级热情，满脸笑容。

494
00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:45.540
And then we're going to have a scene between Esmeralda and Ned.
接下来我们会有埃斯梅拉达和内德之间的一场戏。

495
00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:48.320
And she's got a stack of stories that Marv approved.
她手里有一叠马夫批准的报道。

496
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.520
But Ned's like, wait, I had sort of scrapped some of those.
但内德却说，等等，我本来已经毙掉其中一些了。

497
00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.600
I have a question.
我有个问题。

498
00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:54.040
Yeah.
说吧。

499
00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.460
Why is Ned killing any stories?
为什么内德要毙掉报道？

500
00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:00.780
Do they have so much content that he can just kill stories?
他们的内容多到可以随意毙掉报道吗？

501
00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.780
I feel like we're in a beggars can't be chooser situation here.
我觉得我们现在属于那种没得挑的情况。

502
00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.000
We 100% are.
百分之百是。

503
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:11.820
This whole episode starts with a completely empty dry erase board with the word story ideas and nothing under it.
这一整集开头，白板上写着“故事创意”几个字，下面却空空如也。

504
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:15.380
And I'm like, how are they putting out a newspaper every day?
我就在想，他们到底是怎么做到每天出一份报纸的？

505
00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:20.180
Like, I feel like they would be lucky to have a single weekend paper.
我觉得他们能出一份周末报就不错了。

506
00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.020
Not a Sunday paper, too thick.
不是周日那种太厚的报纸。

507
00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:24.200
A Saturday, once a week paper.
就是那种一周一次的周六报。

508
00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:25.780
A Saturday, here's what's happening around town.
一份周六报，上面写着城里发生了什么事。

509
00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:27.760
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，是这样。

510
00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:30.140
Ned is going to go approach Marv about it.
内德打算去找马夫谈谈这件事。

511
00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.900
And Marv is talking to Kimberly.
当时马夫正在和金伯利说话。

512
00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.980
And as Ned approaches, he's like, hey, buddy, how you doing?
内德走过去说，嘿，伙计，你好吗？

513
00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.040
You know, Kimberly here.
你知道，这是金伯利。

514
00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:39.800
She just sold her one millionth roll of softies.
她刚刚卖出了第一百万卷 Softies 卫生纸。

515
00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:45.400
I noticed she was wearing the sweatshirt with the gray sheep that you pointed out.
我注意到她穿着你指出的那件印有灰色小羊的运动衫。

516
00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:46.320
The softies logo.
那是 Softies 的标志。

517
00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:50.380
Well, Ned is not impressed that she has sold one million rolls.
内德对她卖出一百万卷并不感到惊讶。

518
00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:52.160
But I was.
但我很惊讶。

519
00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:55.300
And it got me going to the internet, lady.
这让我上网查了查，女士。

520
00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.800
What did the internet say?
网上怎么说？

521
00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:01.300
Are you going to tell me, like, how far one million rolls of toilet paper stretches?
你是要告诉我一百万卷卫生纸能铺多长吗？

522
00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:02.260
No, I'm sorry.
不，抱歉。

523
00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:02.740
Is it to the moon?
能铺到月球吗？

524
00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:03.600
No, I'm sorry.
不，抱歉。

525
00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:04.340
I don't know that.
我不知道那个。

526
00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.120
But I did Google real toilet paper salesman.
但我确实谷歌搜索了“真正的卫生纸推销员”。

527
00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.160
Just that.
就搜了这个。

528
00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:09.740
Okay.
好吧。

529
00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:11.500
Real life toilet paper salesman.
现实生活中的卫生纸推销员。

530
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:14.720
And it brought me to one of those AMAs.
然后它把我带到了一个问答帖（AMA）里。

531
00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:16.820
Yeah, you know, online.
对，你知道的，网上的那种。

532
00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:19.260
And I was fascinated by it.
我当时被迷住了。

533
00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.060
What did you learn?
你学到了什么？

534
00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:22.940
I mean, so much.
我是说，学到了很多。

535
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.760
But I'm going to read you just a few things.
但我只读给你听几点。

536
00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:28.740
So this fella started off the AMA with this.
这个家伙在问答帖开头是这么说的。

537
00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:30.040
I am a toilet paper salesman.
我是一名卫生纸推销员。

538
00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:35.260
I manufacture, sell, and distribute private label, bath tissue, paper towels, napkins, and facial tissue.
我生产、销售并分销自有品牌的卫生纸、纸巾、餐巾纸和面巾纸。

539
00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:38.340
People peppered him with all kinds of questions.
人们向他抛出了各种各样的问题。

540
00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:41.140
Also, they did a lot of poop bits.
而且，他们还开了不少关于大便的玩笑。

541
00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:44.400
This guy had to, like, put up with some poop bits.
这家伙不得不忍受一些关于大便的烂梗。

542
00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.140
But here's one for you.
但这里有一个问题给你。

543
00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:53.140
One person said, do you get a lifetime supply of bath tissue, paper towels, napkins, and facial tissue?
有人问，你是不是能终身免费使用卫生纸、纸巾、餐巾纸和面巾纸？

544
00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:55.160
Well, I would think so.
嗯，我觉得应该是。

545
00:22:55.360 --> 00:22:59.120
He said, I actually haven't paid for toilet paper and paper towels in four years.
他说，其实我已经四年没买过卫生纸和纸巾了。

546
00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:02.920
And I live in a house with three other roommates, and we go through quite a bit.
我和另外三个室友住在一起，我们用量相当大。

547
00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:03.860
Wow.
哇。

548
00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:04.920
So there's that.
所以就是这样。

549
00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:11.920
Also, someone said, what ply do you mostly sell, and what is your preferred ply of toilet paper?
还有人问，你们主要卖几层的，你个人偏好几层的卫生纸？

550
00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:15.920
He says that they mostly make two-ply.
他说他们主要生产双层的。

551
00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:17.360
He prefers it as well.
他也更喜欢这种。

552
00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:23.460
The one-ply is for the people who only use one sheet count as the determining factor during the purchase.
单层纸是专门卖给那些只看张数来决定购买的人的。

553
00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:27.760
One-ply is typically a thousand-sheet roll and feels like sandpaper.
单层纸通常是一卷一千张，摸起来像砂纸一样。

554
00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.980
Two-ply is absorbent and soft.
双层纸吸水性好，而且柔软。

555
00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:34.200
And frankly, most two-ply rolls are made as matches to brand names.
坦白说，大多数双层纸卷都是对标知名品牌生产的。

556
00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:38.940
For instance, there are rolls that his company makes for the Family Dollar Store
比如，他公司为“家庭一元店”生产的纸卷，

557
00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:43.860
that are comparable to AngelSoft, which is the number one seller in the U.S.,
品质可以媲美全美销量第一的AngelSoft，

558
00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:45.600
but theirs costs $2 less.
但他们的价格却便宜了2美元。

559
00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:46.840
Huh.
呵。

560
00:23:47.220 --> 00:23:47.500
Huh.
呵。

561
00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:48.080
Right?
对吧？

562
00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:53.680
Also, you might be curious what sort of target demographics they really reach out to
另外，你可能也会好奇他们在做市场营销时，

563
00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:54.920
when they're doing their marketing.
真正瞄准的目标群体是什么样的。

564
00:23:55.980 --> 00:24:00.480
And this fellow said, we target women, mostly ages 20 to 45.
这位仁兄说，我们的目标客户主要是20到45岁的女性。

565
00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:01.940
So you and I are out.
所以你和我都不在目标范围内。

566
00:24:02.480 --> 00:24:02.900
Oh.
哦。

567
00:24:03.060 --> 00:24:03.420
We're out.
我们出局了。

568
00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:05.520
They tend to do the shopping.
她们往往负责家里的购物。

569
00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:08.400
And after 45, Freddie, this is us, Jenna.
而45岁以后，弗雷迪，这就是我们了，珍娜。

570
00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:09.160
What?
什么？

571
00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:11.200
They tend to be stuck in their ways.
她们往往比较固执己见。

572
00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:11.700
Oh.
哦。

573
00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.400
So you're not getting them to buy something new.
所以你很难让她们去买新产品。

574
00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:17.100
Anyway, it was very interesting.
总之，这非常有趣。

575
00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:22.500
And then they talked about how two-ply uses a little bit of glue, you know,
然后他们还谈到了双层纸是怎么用一点胶水，你知道的，

576
00:24:22.580 --> 00:24:27.480
to like make it two-ply and the process and how much money they make
来把它做成双层，以及生产工艺和他们的盈利情况，

577
00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:29.800
and whether something's embossed or have graphics,
还有产品是否压花或印有图案，

578
00:24:29.920 --> 00:24:31.640
what graphics they choose and why.
他们选择什么图案以及原因。

579
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:32.520
It was very interesting.
这真的很有意思。

580
00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:35.300
I'm really attached to my toilet paper.
我对我的卫生纸真的很有感情。

581
00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:36.980
You're exactly what he said.
你完全就是他所说的那种人。

582
00:24:36.980 --> 00:24:42.220
And during the pandemic, when toilet paper wasn't really widely available.
疫情期间，当卫生纸没那么容易买到的时候。

583
00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:42.780
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

584
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.660
And they didn't have my toilet paper for months, for months.
好几个月我都买不到我的那种卫生纸，好几个月啊。

585
00:24:47.320 --> 00:24:52.300
When I finally got my toilet paper back, I took a photo of myself hugging it.
当我终于买回我的卫生纸时，我还拍了一张抱着它的照片。

586
00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:53.200
You sent it to me.
你发给我过。

587
00:24:53.320 --> 00:24:53.660
I know.
我知道。

588
00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:54.700
It's on my camera roll.
还在我的相册里呢。

589
00:24:56.200 --> 00:24:58.340
Wait, what is your TP of choice?
等等，你首选的卫生纸是什么牌子？

590
00:24:58.720 --> 00:24:59.160
Cottonelle.
Cottonelle。

591
00:24:59.660 --> 00:25:00.140
Cottonelle?
Cottonelle？

592
00:25:00.140 --> 00:25:01.340
I don't want Charmin.
我不要Charmin。

593
00:25:01.580 --> 00:25:02.520
I don't want Angel Soft.
我不要Angel Soft。

594
00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:04.800
I don't want any of your other toilet paper.
我不要你们其他的任何卫生纸。

595
00:25:05.020 --> 00:25:07.700
We clearly aren't sponsored by a toilet paper company.
我们显然没有得到任何卫生纸公司的赞助。

596
00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:09.680
Wait, what about it?
等等，它有什么特别的？

597
00:25:09.940 --> 00:25:12.240
I like the little grooves in it.
我喜欢上面那些小凹槽。

598
00:25:12.380 --> 00:25:13.000
The ridges?
你是说纹路？

599
00:25:13.560 --> 00:25:14.080
Yeah.
对。

600
00:25:14.340 --> 00:25:17.060
But I just, it's exactly soft enough.
但我就是觉得，它的柔软度刚刚好。

601
00:25:17.220 --> 00:25:18.100
It's exactly right.
完全正确。

602
00:25:18.280 --> 00:25:19.100
I really like it.
我真的很喜欢它。

603
00:25:19.260 --> 00:25:24.800
If I go stay at like an Airbnb and sometimes even a hotel in any city,
如果我住进爱彼迎，甚至有时候住进任何城市的酒店，

604
00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:29.460
I might, if I'm going to be there long enough, go buy a four-pack of Cottonelle.
如果我要待得够久，我可能会去买一包四卷装的Cottonelle卫生纸。

605
00:25:30.180 --> 00:25:32.560
Because I just, I don't want any other toilet paper.
因为我就是不想用其他任何牌子的卫生纸。

606
00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:34.800
This guy's never selling me his toilet paper.
这家伙永远别想把他的卫生纸卖给我。

607
00:25:34.960 --> 00:25:35.620
He knows that.
他心知肚明。

608
00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:37.120
He's not even going after you.
他甚至都不会来找你推销。

609
00:25:37.320 --> 00:25:37.580
He's not going to bother.
他才懒得费那个劲。

610
00:25:37.980 --> 00:25:38.120
No.
没错。

611
00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:43.060
You know, during the pandemic, Rain was like, I've got a lead on toilet paper.
你知道吗，疫情期间，Rain跟我说，他有卫生纸的货源。

612
00:25:43.220 --> 00:25:44.540
Did I ever tell you this?
我跟你说过这事吗？

613
00:25:44.640 --> 00:25:44.860
No.
没有。

614
00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:45.640
Oh, my God.
天哪。

615
00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:46.820
He texted you?
他给你发短信了？

616
00:25:46.940 --> 00:25:47.860
He texted me.
他给我发了短信。

617
00:25:47.860 --> 00:25:50.340
If you need it, I've got a lead on toilet paper.
如果你需要的话，我有卫生纸的货源。

618
00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:53.220
It's just funny to me that I got that from Rain.
我觉得从Rain那里收到这种消息真是太搞笑了。

619
00:25:53.220 --> 00:25:56.140
And he was like, there's this bamboo toilet paper.
他说，有一种竹浆卫生纸。

620
00:25:56.760 --> 00:25:59.180
And you can get a whole box of it right now.
你现在就能买到整整一箱。

621
00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:00.860
And I was like, you're kidding me.
我当时就想，你在开玩笑吧。

622
00:26:01.020 --> 00:26:02.040
This is amazing.
这太棒了。

623
00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:03.320
We're going to get toilet paper.
我们要有卫生纸用了。

624
00:26:03.760 --> 00:26:05.240
And so I ordered it.
于是我就下单了。

625
00:26:06.040 --> 00:26:08.640
I have never hated a toilet paper more.
我从来没这么讨厌过一种卫生纸。

626
00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:10.500
I hated it so much.
我讨厌透了。

627
00:26:10.740 --> 00:26:11.580
Too grainy?
太粗糙了？

628
00:26:12.100 --> 00:26:14.700
I don't even, I was like, who likes this?
我甚至……我当时就在想，谁会喜欢这个？

629
00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:15.960
I wrote him back angry.
我气冲冲地回了他。

630
00:26:16.240 --> 00:26:16.840
I was like, Rain.
我说，Rain。

631
00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:19.580
You like this?
你喜欢这个？

632
00:26:19.780 --> 00:26:21.420
You like this toilet paper?
你喜欢这种卫生纸？

633
00:26:21.420 --> 00:26:24.700
Like, say it to me, like, with a straight face.
你倒是当着我的面，一本正经地说出来呀。

634
00:26:24.700 --> 00:26:26.240
Like, you're loving this toilet paper.
说你很喜欢这种卫生纸。

635
00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:27.420
He's like, I love it.
他说，我喜欢啊。

636
00:26:27.600 --> 00:26:29.520
I love how it feels.
我喜欢它的触感。

637
00:26:29.520 --> 00:26:30.960
Like, I have no complaints about it.
我完全没觉得有什么问题。

638
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:32.400
I'm like, well, I don't understand you.
我说，好吧，我真是不理解你。

639
00:26:32.580 --> 00:26:34.940
Like, it's a big rift in our friendship, this toilet paper.
这种卫生纸简直成了我们友谊之间的一道鸿沟。

640
00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:35.640
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

641
00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:36.940
He's also a little crunchy.
他也有点怪癖。

642
00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:38.040
I guess so.
我想也是。

643
00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:41.540
Well, anyway, so I didn't want to be wasteful.
总之，我不想浪费。

644
00:26:41.540 --> 00:26:42.660
So I didn't throw it away.
所以我没把它扔掉。

645
00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:46.400
And every once in a while, every once in a while, like...
偶尔，偶尔会有那么……

646
00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:47.580
A roll makes it in.
一卷混了进来。

647
00:26:47.580 --> 00:26:49.840
On our shelf, in our laundry room.
出现在我们洗衣房的架子上。

648
